Presidential elections were held in Austria on 19 April 1998.<ref>[http://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/1757/ Republic of Austria: Election for President] IFES</ref> The result was a victory for the incumbent, President [[Thomas Klestil]], who sought re-election as an independent candidate. The [[Austrian People's Party]], who had originally put him up in [[1992 Austrian presidential election|1992]], reluctantly supported him again, while the [[Austrian Social Democratic Party]] and the [[Austrian Freedom Party]] did not propose any competing candidates. Klestil's competitors were [[Heide Schmidt]], leader of the [[Liberal Forum]], [[Gertraud Knoll]], the former [[Lutheran Church|Lutheran]] [[Superintendent (ecclesiastical)|superintendent]] of [[Burgenland]] (supported by the [[Austrian Green Party|Greens]]), socialite [[Richard Lugner]] and [[Karl Walter Nowak]].

